# Keep the build context small and the image clean. Everything here is either
# rebuilt inside the Dockerfile, machine-local, or a secret.

# Rust build output — hundreds of MB, and a host-built target/ is the wrong
# architecture for the image anyway.
target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node modules are reinstalled from the committed lockfile via `npm ci`.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# The SPA is rebuilt in the frontend stage. A stale host dist/ must never be
# copied in — it would silently ship whatever was last built on a laptop.
dist/
**/dist/
.vite/
**/.vite/

# SQLite lives on the Railway volume, never in the image. The local database is
# ~60 MB plus a ~30 MB WAL, and it sits at backend/mena_ai.db — so these need
# the `**/` prefix. A bare `*.db` is a context-root-only pattern and would have
# shipped ~90 MB to the daemon on every build.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite

# Secrets. Tokens are set as Railway variables and the real file is
# backend/.env, so this also needs `**/` — a bare `.env` matches only the
# context root, where no .env exists.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Git and CI metadata are not needed to build.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Docs — not needed at build or runtime.
README.md
docs/
